configure: include stdlib.h in widechar test

The wide-character feature test calls exit() without including stdlib.h.
GCC 14 treats implicit function declarations as errors, so the test fails,
HAVE_WIDECHAR stays undefined and column.c then misses the wide-char API
(wcspbrk, wprintf).

Signed-off-by: jeep <jeep@local>

--- util-linux-2.26.2.orig/configure.ac	2015-04-30 17:55:42.630681037 +0800
+++ util-linux-2.26.2/configure.ac	2026-10-01 19:52:49.258234091 +0800
@@ -559,6 +559,7 @@
 #include <wchar.h>
 #include <wctype.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 ]], [[
   wchar_t wc;
   wint_t w;
